        "orario": "16:46",
        "timestamp": 1777646803,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Aung San Suu Kyi moved to house arrest Access Asia Issued on: 01/05/2026 - 16:46 Modified: 01/05/2026 - 16:47 This world tour now takes us to Myanmar, where Aung San Suu Kyi will serve the remainder of her sentence under house arrest, following a decision by the head of the ruling junta, now acting as president. The Nobel Peace Prize laureate had until now been held in an undisclosed location. Notion of women as property a 'depravity baked into law', expert says 29/01/2026 Access Asia Thailand's PM sets course for early election amid border and parliamentary unrest 12/12/2025 Access Asia Cambodia retaliates in renewed clashes with Thailand as death toll mounts to 10 09/12/2025 Access Asia Buildings in Bangkok are 'safe to return to' says Thai PM after huge earthquake 28/03/2025 Access Asia Sidelining AfD in German parliament a sign of 'weakness' of traditional parties, analyst says 25/03/2025 Access Asia France investigates founder of adult website linked to mass rape trial: prosecutors 09/01/2025 Access Asia Bangladesh imposes strict curfew with a 'shoot-on-sight-order' following deadly protests 20/07/2024 Access Asia 'This is raising major questions about the policing of this event' 30/10/2022 Access Asia Myanmar coup: 'Generation Z' protesters get creative to make their voices heard 11/02/2021 Access Asia"
